d names him as the only active author and the reviewer to route to, whereas the truth is that nobody active owns any of it. The 4% is under the 10% fail threshold, but Marco is still positioned as the owner.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B credits Marco Silva with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb (117 lines, 19% of exposure). This is the explicit fail condition. It also leaves Marco's two addresses unmerged.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B says the departed share is 89.3%, which is in the 79-90% range. It excludes the Lena Brandt header commit and dependabot's lines. But it gives Peter Scholz 7.9% instead of about 4%, and it has not merged Andrey Subbota's lines. The Peter Scholz figure is far from the truth, so the criterion fails.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C says dblock has the most commits (119) and names Kochnev as the top line owner who left in 2015. It gives dblock about 242 lines, close to the 286 in the truth, which is about 5%. It gives no commit percentages. Kochnev's 756 lines in lib/ and 1,190 across lib/ and spec/ are plausible. It identifies the commits-versus-lines divergence correctly.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives Kochnev 496 lines in exposure, which matches the truth, and lists McCarthy and Yunin as the next authors, both of whom left. It says no active contributor owns the area. But it does not state the active share of at most 8%. It does warn that Marco, Lena and Anna have no real depth, and it routes to Andrei Subbota as a general maintainer, not an expert.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C applies copy detection and returns the grouped_exposure lines to Kochnev. It says Marco's real work is a rename, the copied file and a spec, and Anna made a 5-line change. Marco's share is not stated as a repo percentage, but he is not credited with the code.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C follows delegators back with --follow and credits Kochnev with about 71 surviving lines. That is about 75% of the 67-line... the figure is consistent with the truth. It says everyone in the history is inactive, so no active person owns it, and Marco is not credited with the code.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C says Lena's 20 lines in exposure are copyright headers, but it lists her in the exposure table as an author with 20 lines rather than excluding them. It does not give the departed share of 79-90% or say Subbota's share. It also does not mention dependabot. The departed share is missing, so the criterion fails.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":14695,"type":"result","duration_ms":14717,"uuid":"bb852f38-ce9c-4d7c-a336-3724732d3bfb","ttft_stream_ms":2644,"time_to_request_ms":625,"first_content_frame_ms":2644,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
